</span></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span id="S3.SS3.SSS2.fig1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Figure 4: The sub-manifold multi-scale temporal convolutional layer (MS-TCN), consisting of purely temporal convolutions acting on 4D voxelized space at various kernel sizes, with input voxel resolution <math id="S3.SS3.SSS2.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(T^{\prime},G^{\prime}_{x},G^{\prime}_{y},G^{\prime}_{z})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>G</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>G</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>G</mi><mi>z</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(T^{\prime},G^{\prime}_{x},G^{\prime}_{y},G^{\prime}_{z})</annotation></semantics></math></span>.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S3.SS3.SSS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.SSS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The final two convolutional layers are inspired by the standard residual bottleneck layers of the ResNet architecture <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib44" title="" class="ltx_ref">44</a>]</cite>, but applied in 4D sub-manifold fashion and with a kernel of extent 3 in all axes. The channel matching layer consists of a point-wise convolution to match the output channels for residual addition, as shown in Figure 5.</p>
</div>
